WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.043 --> 00:00:06.910
(breathing heavily)

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:08.213
- [Interviewer] I'm proud of you.

00:00:09.424 --> 00:00:11.000
It takes courage to do this shit.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.570
- Yeah.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.310
I had to muster it up
fucking with a damn tree.

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.340
Just round and around.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:18.173
Then I look down and say,

00:00:18.173 --> 00:00:20.130
"Norman, look at you, stupid dude.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.372
You got on Christmas socks in March."

00:00:22.372 --> 00:00:23.205
(interviewer chuckling)

00:00:23.205 --> 00:00:24.300
- You're wearing green Christmas socks.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.213
- Oh God.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.750
- [Interviewer] All right,
so welcome back, Norman.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:30.583
- Glad to be back.

00:00:30.583 --> 00:00:31.510
- [Interviewer] You were missing,

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:32.610
you were missing in action

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:34.245
for a while here.

00:00:34.245 --> 00:00:35.078
- Yeah.

00:00:35.078 --> 00:00:36.730
- [Interviewer] You were
supposed to show up a couple

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:37.563
of weekends ago for another update,

00:00:37.563 --> 00:00:38.417
- Yeah.

00:00:38.417 --> 00:00:40.485
- [Interviewer] But you didn't show.

00:00:40.485 --> 00:00:41.453
- No, I didn't show up.

00:00:41.453 --> 00:00:44.040
- [Interviewer] That told me
exactly what was going on.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.729
Tell me what you've been through.

00:00:45.729 --> 00:00:46.646
- Well I'm,

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:48.803
I lost my sister.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.623
Dear, dear sister.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:53.573
And I'm--

00:00:53.573 --> 00:00:54.630
- [Interviewer] She died
in an auto accident?

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.863
- Yeah, died in a very
vicious auto accident.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:01.910
Where her head was severed.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:06.039
And, you know, um...

00:01:06.039 --> 00:01:07.800
- [Interviewer] You went to the funeral?

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.037
- Did the funeral and,

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:11.960
that,

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.370
that people they just wanna lambast you

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:16.290
and things like that.

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:18.160
Combination of that and

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:19.960
trying to deal with the emotions and

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:23.190
it just, I couldn't take it anymore.

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:26.030
So I went and I got high
as a motherfucker and

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:27.203
I continued to get high.

00:01:27.203 --> 00:01:28.530
I think in about,

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:29.690
time is it?

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:31.420
I think in about four hours or

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:34.493
four to six hours I have like 24 hours.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.570
Of course I'm ashamed about it and I think

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:40.760
it was me I put,

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:42.790
I put a little bit too much on myself.

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:44.600
It's not so much that I have that,

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:46.420
that I got this feeling.

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:47.630
It's just that.

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:50.340
Okay, today's okay,
just keep going forward.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:54.410
I try my best with the positivity
and everything within me.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:55.623
Even my wherewithal.

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:58.150
And I questioned myself

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:02.050
about five nights ago, "Where
the fuck is your wherewithal?

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:04.550
What the fuck are you doing?

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:07.620
For Christ sakes right now
I have on Christmas socks,

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:09.200
in March."

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.710
And some people might deem that funny but

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:13.683
to me, that's a fucking shame.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.790
I'm

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.610
I don't use anything as an excuse.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:24.023
I believe that excuses are skins
of reasons wrapped in lies.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:25.813
You know,

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:28.033
and basically,

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:32.143
I used because I wanted to.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.343
Because the evidence is, is quite clear.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:40.950
Driven by

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:42.733
a negative emotional status.

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:47.403
Driven by the loss of a loved one.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:51.930
This disease itself is unique
enough to come together

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:54.123
and combine itself and fuck me up.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:57.773
Coming to see you,

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.440
I went around the tree for four times

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.890
'cause I didn't want to come here.

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:03.723
- [Interviewer] Shame.

00:03:03.723 --> 00:03:05.170
- Yeah.

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:06.003
I am,

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.327
I'm pretty, probably really not gonna like

00:03:08.327 --> 00:03:11.770
any of the comments that are negative

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:12.673
but that's okay.

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:17.310
Because I gotta stay in that mind frame

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:19.360
that it's going to get better.

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.560
I remember you were talking about

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:23.210
two steps forward, one step back.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:26.206
Well God damn it I'm tired of stepping.

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:27.039
(giggles)

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:27.872
You know?

00:03:27.872 --> 00:03:29.797
I mean, and, and, and some people may say,

00:03:29.797 --> 00:03:30.790
"Well if you're so tired,

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:32.640
why don't you just stop?"

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:36.120
God damn it it's not that damn easy.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:37.860
- [Interviewer] I think it's
the hardest thing anyone ever

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.051
could ever, could ever do.

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:40.130
- You know,

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:42.083
job wise, everything's just fine.

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:44.310
You know,

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:45.900
there wasn't a cloud on the horizon

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:48.757
as "The Big Book of
Alcoholics, Anonymous" states.

00:03:48.757 --> 00:03:53.610
And,

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.780
unconsciously I knew it,

00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:56.880
but it didn't suffice.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.200
Because I got real shaky

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.570
before I drank.

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:02.510
I drank first

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:05.430
and then I went and got some crack in.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:07.780
I've even tried crystal meth.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.180
No I don't really like that shit.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:11.340
But, you know as

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:18.160
as devastated as I may be,
I gotta pick my head up.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:19.640
I gotta keep going forward.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:21.400
I gotta muster up the wherewithal.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.660
I gotta keep praying.

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:24.160
I gotta still keep believing,

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.400
I still gotta have that faith.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.710
You know that not
knowing untouchable faith

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:30.290
I have to have it.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.590
You know, I was put in
some situations while I was

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:33.840
you know, running around.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:36.800
Well they weren't death-defying,

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:38.780
you know, but I had to fight.

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:39.767
You know, and

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.800
I don't like to fight because

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.010
when I fight,

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.790
every time I fight I see my mother

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:47.993
laying in a casket.

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:50.550
And

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:51.823
that's all I remember.

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:54.883
I see mom.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:58.130
And it's like a

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:58.963
black.

00:04:58.963 --> 00:05:00.320
It's just,

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.523
this guy told me, he said,
"Man," he said, "Dude,

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:08.020
I've never seen anybody fight like that."

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:09.450
I said, "What happened?"

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:11.140
He said, "What, what happened?"

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:12.360
He said, "Look."

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:14.050
This guy was laying on
the ground with blood

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:15.923
coming out of his ears and his nose.

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:18.840
And I got the hell away from over there.

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:22.190
I could have killed that guy.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.423
All about drugs.

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:29.470
He wanted to hit and I told him no.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:30.433
I remember that.

00:05:32.097 --> 00:05:33.660
(breathing heavily)

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:35.660
What if the situation was turned around?

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:39.660
What if that would have been me?

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:41.820
What if I would've hit
my head on the pavement?

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:42.970
That was all she wrote.

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:46.880
So I just I'm...

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:53.923
At this point I really don't know,

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:58.150
but I know I'm gonna know

00:05:58.150 --> 00:05:58.983
soon.

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:03.380
I really thank God for keeping me

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:07.153
with some semblance of
sanity while I was out there.

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:12.410
Last night was the first time

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:14.063
I really had a comfortable sleep.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:18.030
'Cause I've had to keep one eye open.

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:20.940
I was down here on Skid
Row for a minute and

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:22.060
I went to other places because

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:23.490
I didn't want anybody to find me.

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:24.680
Lo and behold,

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:27.140
when I come back to fucking
Skid Row somebody sees me.

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:28.770
- [Interviewer] You were in a,

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:29.770
they put you up in a place for a while.

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:30.650
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:31.483
I was there.

00:06:31.483 --> 00:06:32.710
Yeah. I was in a,

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:34.400
place before I moved into the

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:35.650
the transitional home.

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:37.080
And everything was fine.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:38.170
You know,

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:40.840
I even seen the drug deal in the motel

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:42.090
go down.

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:43.960
But I'm like, "Hmm,"

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:44.867
it's not that I just

00:06:44.867 --> 00:06:47.620
you know brush it off like,
"Shit I got this." No.

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:49.297
I was like, "Wow."

00:06:49.297 --> 00:06:50.900
You know, that's something.

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:51.733
No thought.

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:56.380
I'm not going to ask myself "Why?"

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:57.970
Anymore.

00:06:57.970 --> 00:06:59.623
Because God damn it, I know why.

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:02.780
Bottom line is, I'm an addict.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:05.620
The bottom line is I have

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:08.000
a mind as you may see me how

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.930
you may, you may see.

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:12.960
People may think that
I'm brilliant as hell.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:14.873
Yeah, I have some book sense.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.863
And I have some street sense.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.170
But I have to really put this in my mind,

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:23.883
there's times when I have no sense.

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:27.070
My mind has the capability

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:28.870
of fucking me without my permission.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:33.640
And it's unique that it always does this

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:36.390
when things are okay.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:38.260
- [Interviewer] You understand
that everyone does though.

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:40.760
- And I'm beginning to
learn that because I seen

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:43.950
a couple of people that
were in recovery with me

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:45.330
at certain times,

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:46.163
and uh

00:07:47.350 --> 00:07:48.950
one of the guys, we sat down and

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:51.390
he said, "Man, I'm tired of doing this."

00:07:51.390 --> 00:07:53.240
I said, "I am too, but I can't stop."

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:55.202
He said, "You too?"

00:07:55.202 --> 00:07:56.310
I said, "Yap"

00:07:56.310 --> 00:07:58.180
I said "The moment I said, I wanna stop,

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:00.430
I'll get up, walk down the
street and hear somebody say

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:02.077
Hey, do this, do that."

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:06.423
There's not too much to say.

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:11.460
But I know it's a whole lot to do.

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:16.100
That's the bereavement time.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:17.550
So I'm okay.

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:19.033
As far as that's concerned.

00:08:19.033 --> 00:08:20.317
And then I asked myself last night,

00:08:20.317 --> 00:08:22.317
"Do I really want to go back to the job?

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:24.317
Do I really need to go back--"

00:08:24.317 --> 00:08:25.540
- [Interviewer] So you
didn't lose the job?

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:26.437
- No.

00:08:26.437 --> 00:08:27.417
"Do I really?"

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:30.463
- [Interviewer] How did
you not lose your job?

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:33.130
- Because they knew
about the, I told them.

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:35.010
Flat out about the bereavement.

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:35.843
And,

00:08:35.843 --> 00:08:37.120
they said, "Okay,

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:38.120
well

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:39.570
you're new."

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:42.100
But you know, they offered
me some, some time off.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:43.030
Some bereavement time.

00:08:43.030 --> 00:08:44.090
And I was like, "Cool."

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:44.961
I mean, 'cause I worked for a company man

00:08:44.961 --> 00:08:46.690
that's really cool.

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:47.523
- [Interviewer] Because
of your sister's death,

00:08:47.523 --> 00:08:48.356
they gave you time off.

00:08:48.356 --> 00:08:49.189
- Yes.
- [Interviewer] Got it.

00:08:49.189 --> 00:08:50.150
- And I'm,

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:53.070
I mean, you know, I went
to the, I think I text you.

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:54.000
I went to the main office

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.400
and everybody stood up and applaud me.

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:57.440
I'm like, "What the fuck is going on?"

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:59.570
Well somebody seen my
story and they told someone

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:01.130
and then they told someone,

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:02.110
and they all watched it.

00:09:02.110 --> 00:09:03.820
And then a couple of
the ladies were in tears

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:06.597
and they just looked at me like, you know,

00:09:06.597 --> 00:09:07.943
"you're so encouraging.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:13.330
You're such a

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:15.430
breath of fresh air. You're such a light."

00:09:19.499 --> 00:09:20.670
(sighs)

00:09:20.670 --> 00:09:21.503
Wow.

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:23.600
As many.

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:24.950
- [Interviewer] And you stay alive.

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:27.500
- Many positive things that I receive.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.340
There's times when

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:31.060
the negative dominates.

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:32.660
And this was one of those times.

00:09:36.979 --> 00:09:37.979
When you pick it up,

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:41.096
it's gonna get better.

00:09:41.096 --> 00:09:43.146
I may have another setback, I don't know.

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:47.110
I'm not going to deal
with a predictable mind.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:50.780
But I am going to take things

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:51.930
a hell of a lot slower.

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:55.920
A hell of a lot slower to give myself

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:57.080
ample time to

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:02.150
understand

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:05.210
that "Motherfucker you're
not out of the fucking water

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:06.957
just because things are okay."

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:11.123
I know I put too much on myself.

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:16.123
I don't believe ego and pride set in.

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:19.010
Pride only set in when I just

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:21.291
tried to walk down this
damn street and I was,

00:10:21.291 --> 00:10:22.913
I was like, "No, man,

00:10:22.913 --> 00:10:24.219
I won't disappoint Mark."

00:10:24.219 --> 00:10:25.950
But see, it's not

00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:26.976
on the bus ride over here,

00:10:26.976 --> 00:10:28.899
it's not about disappointing people.

00:10:28.899 --> 00:10:30.732
And it's not about disappointing me.

00:10:30.732 --> 00:10:32.263
(siren wailing)

00:10:32.263 --> 00:10:34.037
It's the fact that I
got to understand that

00:10:34.037 --> 00:10:36.410
"Motherfucker you're an addict.

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:37.453
And this shit happens.

00:10:37.453 --> 00:10:39.820
(siren wailing)

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:42.449
Maybe there'll come a time
where it won't happen again."

00:10:42.449 --> 00:10:44.900
(siren wailing)

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:46.350
We take the bitter with the sweet.

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:48.133
We do what we need to do,

00:10:48.133 --> 00:10:49.444
and we keep moving forward.

00:10:49.444 --> 00:10:51.030
That's all I can give.

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:53.235
(siren wailing)

00:10:53.235 --> 00:10:55.270
- [Interviewer] Losing your sister was

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:56.110
a serious

00:10:57.780 --> 00:10:58.613
you know,

00:10:58.613 --> 00:11:00.093
it's a hard thing to go through.

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:02.490
And the relapse is

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:03.670
almost

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:04.516
- Inevitable.

00:11:04.516 --> 00:11:05.349
(Norman laughing)
- [Interviewer] Inevitable.

00:11:05.349 --> 00:11:06.626
I mean, it's just

00:11:06.626 --> 00:11:07.459
